#: /home/cvs/prod/branches/KDE/4.2/kdebase/workspace/khotkeys/data/kde32b1.khotkeys:439
msgctxt "Comment"
msgid ""
"After pressing Alt+Ctrl+H, 'Hello' input will be simulated just like if you "
"typed it. Especially useful if you're lazy to type things like 'unsigned'. "
"Every keypress in the input is separated by a colon ':' . Note that the "
"keypresses mean really keypresses, so you have to write what you'd really "
"press on the keyboard. In the table below, left column shows the input and "
"the right column shows what to type.\\n\\n\"enter\" (i.e. new "
"line)                Enter or Return\\na (i.e. small "
"a)                          A\\nA (i.e. capital a)                       "
"Shift+A\\n: (colon)                                  Shift+;\\n' "
"'  (space)                              Space"
msgstr ""

#: /home/cvs/prod/branches/KDE/4.2/kdebase/workspace/khotkeys/data/kde32b1.khotkeys:485
msgctxt "Name"
msgid "Type 'Hello'"
msgstr "Напишете „Здраво“"

